      "hints": [
        "Find the coefficient of $x^4$ in the expansion of $(x+a)^6$: $\\binom{6}{2} x^4 a^2 = 15a^2$, so $p = 15a^2$.",
        "Find the coefficient of $x^2$ in the expansion of $(ax+3)^4$: $\\binom{4}{2} (ax)^2 (3^2) = 6 \\times 9 a^2 = 54a^2$, so $q = 54a^2$.",
        "Set up the equation $p + q = 276 \\implies 15a^2 + 54a^2 = 276$ and solve for $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the $x^4$ term in the binomial expansion of $(x + a)^6$:\n$$\\binom{6}{2} x^4 a^2 = 15a^2 x^4 \\implies p = 15a^2$$",
        "Determine the $x^2$ term in the binomial expansion of $(ax + 3)^4$:\n$$\\binom{4}{2} (ax)^2 (3^2) = 6 \\cdot a^2 x^2 \\cdot 9 = 54a^2 x^2 \\implies q = 54a^2$$",
        "Form the equation using $p + q = 276$:\n$$15a^2 + 54a^2 = 276 \\implies 69a^2 = 276$$",
        "Solve for the possible values of $a$:\n$$a^2 = \\frac{276}{69} = 4 \\implies a = \\pm 2$$"
      ],
